'''Jev Eremia''' was a [[human]] [[Jedi]] who was a [[youngling]] in [[132 BBY]] during the [[High Republic Era]]. He attended a lesson in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]] led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]], who had the students [[Meditation|meditate]] and connect with [[the Force]]. Eremia saw the Force as a [[fire]], consuming all that tried to stop it, and Sol explained that the Force was a power that must be respected. He then dismissed the class for [[Foodstuff|lunch]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Connect to the Force. Have faith. Think of diving into a great ocean. Give yourselves over to its weight, its stillness, its uncertainty. And tell me what comes into your mind.|Sol instructs Eremia and his class|audio=Sol-ConnectToTheForce-LostFound.flac|<ref name="LostFound" />}}
[[File:JevEremia-LostFound.png|thumb|right|300px|alt=Jev Eremia, wearing tan Jedi robes, sits with his eyes closed on the floor of a training veranda in the Coruscant Jedi Temple.|Jev Eremia was a Jedi youngling on Coruscant during the High Republic Era.]]
Jev Eremia was a [[human]] member of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> In [[132 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> he<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> was still a [[youngling]] and attended a lesson led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Sol]] on a training veranda in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. During the lesson, Eremia sat cross-legged on the floor with the rest of the class as Sol instructed them to close their [[eye]]s, explaining that sight could not be trusted as it could be deceived. Instead, he had the [[Meditation|meditating]] [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] connect to [[the Force]] and tell him what entered their minds.<ref name="LostFound" />

After other students called out what they saw, Eremia stated that he saw a growing [[fire]], consuming everything that stood against it. Sol nodded and explained that the Force was powerful like a fire or an [[ocean]] and so must be respected. Seeing the Jedi Master [[Vernestra Rwoh]] waiting to speak with him, Sol then called the lesson to an end and Eremia and the other students opened their eyes and stood. As they filed out of the veranda for [[Foodstuff|lunch]], shepherded by<ref name="LostFound" /> [[Jedi Knight]] [[Flurri Wiss]]<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> and another [[Jedi]], each of them bowed before Rwoh.<ref name="LostFound" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|The Force is powerful. Like fire or the ocean. It is a power we must respect.|Sol responds to Eremia's vision of the Force|audio=Sol-PowerfulForce-LostFound.flac|<ref name="LostFound" />}}
During meditation, Jev Eremia perceived the Force as a flame that had to be respected for its destructive potential, but that could be nurturing and warming if carefully tended. He had dark skin, [[Color|black]] [[hair]], and brown eyes.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Equipment==
During his lesson with Sol, Eremia wore tan [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] with a brown [[belt]] and brown shoes.<ref name="LostFound" /> The belt's gray buckle bore a seal of the late High Republic.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Behind the scenes==
Jev Eremia was portrayed by [[Jeremiah Evans]] in "[[Lost / Found]],"<ref name="LostFound" /> the first episode of the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="Announcement">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-teaser-poster|text=''The Acolyte'' Teaser Poster, Premiere Date Revealed}}</ref> Prior to the release of the episode, he was revealed in a trailer exclusively shown at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="CelebrationDate">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> The scenes in the Jedi Temple were shot at [[Shinfield Studios]],<ref name="Fantha Part I">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Julian Foddy">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=''The Acolyte'' Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy}}</ref> The character was credited only as "youngling" in the episode<ref name="LostFound" /> and he was first named in the [[2025]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

